<aura:documentation>
	<aura:description>

    <p>Redux Reducer Base Component</p>

    <!-- LAST UPDATED DATE / VERSION -->
    <p>Last Updated: 3/12/2019</p>
    <p>CurrentVersion: 3.0</p>
    <hr/>
    <!-- UPDATE DATE / VERSION WITH ANY UPDATES -->


        <p><a href="https://redux.js.org/basics/reducers">Redux Reducers</a></p>
        <p>This is the base component for the reducers related to the <code>ISGRedux</code> component.</p>
        <p>See the documentation for ISGRedux for an overview of the Redux setup.</p>
        <hr/>
        <p>Reducer subcomponents containing a slice of the Redux app state extend this base component.</p>
        <p>Steps to create a reducer subcomponent:</p>
        <p>(This example is a store for holding user state / info)</p>
        <ul>
            <li>STEP 1: Create a Lightning Component ie. "ReducerForUserData" that extends <code>ReducerBase</code></li>
            <pre>&lt;aura:component extends="c:ISGReducerBase"&gt;&lt;/aura:component&gt;</pre>
            <li>In the helper js file specify a <code>getReducer</code> function:</li>
            <pre>getReducer : function() {
  return function(state, action) {

    // Initial State
    if (!state) state = {
      items: [],
      notificationMessage: ''
    };

    switch(action.type) {

      case 'clearCompareTray':
        return Object.assign({}, state, { items: [], notificationMessage: '' });

      default:
        return state;
    }
  };
},</pre>

            <li>
              <p>NOTE! Always return a new object clone of the original state value in helper action functions.</p>
              <p>Use: <code>Object.assign({} ...)</code> or <code>.slice()</code> etc...</p>
            </li>
            <li>STEP 3: Connect the reducer to the <code>ISGRedux</code> base component by adding it as a child component with aura:id="reducer" and storeName="..." attributes.</li>
          <pre>&lt;c:ReducerForUserData aura:id="reducer" storeName="UserData" /&gt;</pre>
        </ul>

        <br/>

        <p>Caching (getCacheFormatter)</p>
        <p>Another function is possible to override in the helper which controls what parts of the state gets cached to LocalStorage.</p>
        <p>Example Usage:</p>
        <pre>getCacheFormatter: function() {
  return function(state) {
    return Object.assign({}, state, {
      notificationMessage: ''
    });
  };
},</pre>

